.TH SHB-SECRET 1 "October 2026" "SecretHarbor 0.4.0-prod" "SecretHarbor Manual"
.SH NAME
shb-secret \- Manage credentials and broker capabilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshb secret <list|status|test|set|delete> [key] [val]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects capability states, allowed hosts, and vault metadata. Intentionally does NOT provide commands to reveal or dump raw secret values.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBdelete\fR
Deletes a credential from the encrypted local vault.
.TP
\fBlist\fR
Lists all secret keys currently registered in the encrypted local vault or policy broker.
.TP
\fBset\fR
Encrypts and stores a credential in AES-256-GCM vault with strict file permissions.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Displays agent visibility, runtime capability injection state, allowed outbound hosts, and storage provider without revealing secret contents.
.TP
\fBtest\fR
Validates presence in the local vault, tests synthetic fake value generation, and checks broker routing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
$ \fBshb secret list\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb secret status DATABASE_URL\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb secret test STRIPE_KEY\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb secret set STRIPE_KEY sk_live_...\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb secret delete STRIPE_KEY\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
shb(1)
.SH WEBSITE
https://secretharbor.dev
